              "year": "1979",
              "unstructured": "Meicenheimer, R.D. (1979) Am. J. Botany 66, 557\u2013569.",
              "journal-title": "Am. J. Botany"
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR24",
              "unstructured": "In the geometrical model the positions of the particles are a priori fixed on an artificial generative spiral: \u03b8(n)=n\u03d5, R(n)=Roexp(nH)."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR25",
              "unstructured": "It is equivalent to say (Ref. 3) that the appearance order of the two neighbours of the new particle n are n-i and n-j, and that the parastichies numbers are (i, j)."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR26",
              "doi-asserted-by": "publisher",
              "first-page": "533",
              "DOI": "10.1209/0295-5075/14/6/006",
              "volume": "14",
              "author": "LS Levitov",
              "year": "1991",
              "unstructured": "Levitov, L.S. (1991) Europhys. Lett. 14, 533\u2013539.",
              "journal-title": "Europhys. Lett."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR27",
              "unstructured": "Note that the same dynamical selection of the bifurcations is obtained. The condition on the new place is now not to be the largest one but the first available one."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR28",
              "unstructured": "The resulting G can be compared with the geometrical prediction for the value of G around which this mode would be observed: Gd = 1/4 ln[3] \u2248 0.275."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR29",
              "doi-asserted-by": "publisher",
              "first-page": "63",
              "DOI": "10.1098/rstb.1935.0007",
              "volume": "225",
              "author": "M Snow",
              "year": "1935",
              "unstructured": "Snow, M. and Snow, R. (1935) Phil. Trans. Roy. Soc. London Ser. B 225, 63\u201394.",
              "journal-title": "Phil. Trans. Roy. Soc. London Ser. B"
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR30",
              "unstructured": "The diference between the plastochrone ratio measured by Richards, and the value of exp(G) for which we observe the decussate mode comes from the fact that, for a quantitative comparition between theory and botany, the exact form of the primordia must be taken into account (see ref 12 and 32)."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR31",
              "first-page": "301",
              "volume": "25",
              "author": "WW Schwabe",
              "year": "1971",
              "unstructured": "Schwabe, W. W. (1971) Soc. Exp. Biol. Symp. 25, 301, 322.",
              "journal-title": "Soc. Exp. Biol. Symp."
            },
            {
              "key": "36_CR32",
